  "question": {
    "text": "A large number of water drops, each of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, combine to have a drop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. If the surface tension is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> and mechanical equivalent of heat is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi></math>, the rise in heat energy per unit volume will be:"
